    "summary": "The requested execution completed (receipt dd59f37872d240548eff168eb821901f, exit 0) and its primary comparison is answered from the retained observations, so the shouldSnapshot question is now explained with a measured interpretation.\n\nConfirmed defect (interpretation tied to experiment 0620c91eb9c641de9723369bd4729fd6-experiment): the automatic snapshot condition of a node that recovered through InstallSnapshot is permanently true while the node is idle, so it keeps writing fresh snapshots of unchanged state. Receipt evidence, parsed indices: index 0 recovery_state shows the snapshot index advancing 62→202 across the reconnect while the log store last index stayed 62 (log_store_below_snapshot_index true, snapshot_advanced_over_log_store true); index 1 window_start for that node shows should_snapshot true with snapshot index 202 and log store last index 62; index 3 recovered_window_end after 22 samples at 40ms reports applied_delta 0, distinct_snapshot_ids 15, snapshot_created_without_new_entries true, newest snapshot index still 202 while the newest ID moved from 2-202-1791708222798 to 2-202-1791708223751 — comparison_index 0 holds with the victim_window admission matched at index 1. Mechanism from source: shouldSnapshot (snapshot.go:106-120) subtracts the log store's own LastIndex from the snapshot index as unsigned with no ordering guard, while installSnapshot (raft.go:1814-1950) sets the snapshot index above the surviving log store index after compaction bounded by min(snapIdx, lastLogIdx-trailingLogs) (snapshot.go:216-240), and runSnapshots (snapshot.go:72-102) samples that condition every SnapshotInterval. takeSnapshot still succeeds because the FSM index equals the installed snapshot index (snapshot.go:125-211). Consequence stated as repeated avoidable snapshot work (IO and FSM Snapshot() cost), not a safety or availability failure; snapshot retention still bounds stored copies. Gap-2 is answered and the question is marked explained.\n\nControl caveat handled honestly: in that receipt the leader's control comparison came back unknown ('No corresponding prerequisite events reached: control_window/window_start') because both nodes emitted one shared end-event name, so the control is supported only by the operands recorded in the same receipt (indices 2 and 4: should_snapshot false, log store index equal to snapshot index, 1 distinct snapshot ID at index 202 with applied_delta 0). A successor experiment is therefore requested with previous_id 0620c91eb9c641de9723369bd4729fd6-experiment, a documented revision reason, and a harness that differs only in event naming (recovered_window_end / control_window_start / control_window_end) with identical producers, configuration and window; the local run of that successor reproduced the same split (15 vs 1 distinct IDs). Validation of these bytes returns valid:true."
